# Windows script line endings.
#
# The offline bundle's launcher is a .cmd, and cmd.exe parses batch files expecting CRLF. An LF-only
# .cmd mostly works by luck on a short script and then fails in a way that is very hard to read --
# `goto` labels and multi-line `if` blocks are the usual casualties. Pin these to CRLF in the
# repository so a fresh clone cannot produce one.
#
# This does not conflict with the other thing that has to be true for those files: 启动.cmd must stay
# pure ASCII and launch.ps1 must keep its UTF-8 BOM, both enforced by
# tools/offline-bundle/fix-encoding.ps1. Git normalises line endings; it does not touch a BOM, and it
# leaves ASCII alone.
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf